                        "entry_id": "7abc2031-1eb2-34d4-845a-e04a5e48d3fa",
                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… романизи́ровать"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "86b1aff6-5815-3cce-8e10-0b9a0a8ec3d9",
                        "entry_id": "7abc2031-1eb2-34d4-845a-e04a5e48d3fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. изменять (изменить) кого-либо, что-либо по древнеримскому образцу; вводить (ввести) в чей-либо быт, укоренять (укоренить) где-либо язык, культуру и обычаи Древнего Рима"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "164ad161-9a67-49ab-87c9-efb639d25250",
                                "sense_id": "86b1aff6-5815-3cce-8e10-0b9a0a8ec3d9",
                                "text": "С одной стороны, чтобы оставаться на гребне волны и господствовать, церковь «романизирует» своё христианство; с другой стороны, она противится новой действительности, она хочет устранить её и подчинить себе империю."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8696fe10-a079-4a08-89be-6680ed2ad041",
                        "source_entry_id": "7abc2031-1eb2-34d4-845a-e04a5e48d3fa",
                        "source_sense_id": "86b1aff6-5815-3cce-8e10-0b9a0a8ec3d9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Romanize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Romanize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2536b753-52ea-3a5b-994c-dca45cf49cef",
                                        "entry_id": "a588c78b-503a-3d9b-8ceb-88b35cb4ff3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of romanize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eaeee5e1-cf53-4b60-8b99-e460d0c9b0db",
                                                "sense_id": "2536b753-52ea-3a5b-994c-dca45cf49cef",
                                                "text": "‘We don’t like their categorization system,’ explained Anthony. ‘It only makes sense in Roman characters, but not every language is so easily Romanized, is it?’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Romanize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c027c107-fb41-3c60-92ee-2aa84733b845",
                                        "entry_id": "5c2470b4-c54b-35fa-9321-8f434993e6f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To Romanianize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52dccc27-202b-43d0-a20f-153dc7453edf",
                                                "sense_id": "c027c107-fb41-3c60-92ee-2aa84733b845",
                                                "text": "On the surface, the current debate in Transylvania has to do with minority rights and local issues, like the re-establishment of those Hungarian language schools that had been 'Romanized' by Nicolae Ceausescu, the late dictator."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d789d0bc-f8cc-49c5-8922-c2eaf14d3982",
                                                "sense_id": "c027c107-fb41-3c60-92ee-2aa84733b845",
                                                "text": "The Romanian Communist Party also decided to extensively Romanize the cities of Transylvania through a slow, but inexorable policy of reducing Hungarian cultural identity and autonomy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
